            {
              "id": "87deeccf-9a01-4106-b69e-065d6a23537f",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Mind, Self, &amp; Society from the Standpoint of a Social Behaviorist</strong></em> was written by George Herbert Mead, published by The University of Chicago Press, August 15, 1967."
            },
            {
              "id": "9fafcf5b-ad56-43e5-84c2-9d0d67e6e971",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "441e4a8b-0a96-4c66-b484-d704feb2dee1",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Written from the standpoint of the social behaviorist, this </em><a href=\"#/treatise-voyage\"><em>treatise</em></a><em> contains the heart of Mead's position on social psychology. The analysis of </em><a href=\"#/the-game-of-language\"><em>language</em></a><em> is of major interest, as it supplied for the first time an adequate treatment of the language mechanism in relation to scientific and philosophical issues.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "293afb9a-42f3-4713-9d31-52fb28f7d1da",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
